{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"placement"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","text":"MXLAboveBelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"placement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/placement","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"notation."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/placement"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"placement","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV9placementAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgvp","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","text":"MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"title":"MXLAboveBelow","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/placement":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/placement","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/placement","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"placement"}}}